  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Client boundaries",
      "items": [
        "views contains shared pages; core owns API, Query hooks and client stores; ui owns primitives.",
        "Mobile owns its UI, hooks and state; only core types and pure utilities are shared.",
        "Docs and UI Lab support development; they are outside this runtime path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Control and persistence",
      "items": [
        "The API authorizes requests and owns durable task claims. Claims check runtime binding and concurrency inside a transaction.",
        "Daemon claims use WebSocket RPC first, with conditional HTTP fallback and a safety delay after uncertain outcomes.",
        "Reports return to the API; completion endpoint: server/internal/daemon/client.go:621-645."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Execution context",
      "items": [
        "The daemon prepares the environment before invoking a provider adapter. The agent process receives a working directory.",
        "Fresh task directories start empty; repository checkout is on demand. Local-directory and worktree modes also exist.",
        "Worker files are separate from server attachment storage. Task scoping does not imply an OS security sandbox."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Optional capabilities and scope",
      "items": [
        "Redis enables cross-node realtime relay when configured; server/cmd/server/main.go:448-456, 575-576.",
        "Plugin hooks are mediated by the daemon API; server/cmd/server/router.go:1567-1573. Plugin surfaces run off the authenticated origin: 1729-1732.",
        "This is a code-backed system overview, not a live deployment inventory. Provider internals, individual endpoints and integration transports are omitted."
      ]
    }
  ]
